# SEO, Accessibility and Performance Standards

Follow `docs/architecture/seo-performance-strategy.md`.

Rules:

- Keep the landing static-first whenever possible.
- Keep public content renderable in the initial HTML.
- Use one `h1` per page.
- Sections should use semantic HTML and `aria-labelledby` when titled.
- Informative images need meaningful `alt`.
- Decorative images use `alt=""` and `aria-hidden`.
- Use `next/image` for raster images in React components.
- Use `priority` only for real above-the-fold LCP candidates.
- Images below the fold should keep default lazy loading.
- Reserve image dimensions or aspect ratio to avoid CLS.
- Third-party scripts must be lazy, isolated, and loaded with `next/script` when added.
- Do not add analytics until tracking, privacy and consent strategy are clear.
